        id: 'm-a-006-b',
        text: 'A clinician conducts a comprehensive assessment that includes a functional analysis, neuropsychological testing, trauma history review, and genetic screening before proposing any hypothesis about the function of a child\'s problem behavior, wanting to ensure all possible variables are considered.',
